ion_type":"conceptual","question":"What does half-life summarize?","options":["The maximum possible lifetime","The exact first arrival count","The probability of two independent events.","The time by which survival has fallen to half."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fda046746cba92d978edc00c"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For exponential decay with rate $\\lambda$, what is the half-life?","options":["$1/\\lambda$","$\\lambda/\\log(2)$","$\\log(2)/\\lambda$","$2\\lambda$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2ccaf0f41bf470d2aee3f372"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"In exponential waiting models, what distribution summary is half-life?","options":["A variance only","A maximum value","A median survival time","A count parameter"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a29373291e9cc640958ac0b4"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If a drug concentration decays exponentially, what is its half-life?","options":["The time until the concentration is halved","The time until concentration doubles","The initial concentration","The variance of concentration"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e5e3b2ef99c76b8dbf82fc06"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Radioactive decay half-life summarizes what?","options":["The number of stable atoms initially","The exact time every atom decays","The sample maximum of lifetimes","How quickly unstable atoms decay"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d6dcc2bc7cd557f9a4e02400"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $\\lambda=2$, what is the exponential half-life?","options":["$2\\log(2)$","$\\log(2)/2$","$1/2$","$2$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d89d3ba55f053c26d78fdd69"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $S_X(5)=1/2$, what can be said about $5$?","options":["It is the mean necessarily","It is the variance necessarily","It is a half-life","It is outside the support"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fc6e9082757072ca80181a50"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What does a shorter half-life indicate?","options":["Faster decay or faster event occurrence","Slower decay","No decay","A larger median survival time"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e845232a6621bae01fdf8a85"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is half-life easy to communicate?","options":["It requires knowing every density value.","It is always the same as variance","It is a negative time","The time until half remains or half have survived."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9b62e3cf936072465d27de54"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How is half-life related to the median for survival times?","options":["It is the largest possible survival time.","The time by which survival probability is one half.","It is always the mean waiting time","It is unrelated to quantiles"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"47aab1f8750796c713c69596"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why is exponential half-life smaller when $\\lambda$ is larger?","options":["$\\log(2)/\\lambda$ increases as $\\lambda$ increases","The survival function becomes negative","$\\log(2)/\\lambda$ decreases as $\\lambda$ increases","Half-life does not depend on $\\lambda$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"0f13ba74a03e8ac4df74b246"},{"id":"pt_batch10_half_life_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $\\lambda=0.5$, what is t